  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lumen Technologies Government Solutions obligated $295M in federal contract dollars in FY2026 to date. Lumen Technologies Government Solutions won 348 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $846K. Obligations are down 30.3% year over year. The largest buyers so far are the Department of Veterans Affairs ($75.5M), the Department of Defense ($55.2M), the Department of Agriculture ($50.7M) and the Department of the Interior ($50.2M). Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the dominant market, with reported obligations of $252M, $42.9M and $16K across listed entries, and Other Computer Related Services shows $32.7K. Obligations by fiscal year show a rise from $102M in FY21 to a peak of $423M in FY25, then $295M in FY26. The data are partial because FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date. This summary focuses on obligations, award counts, top buying agencies, and the NAICS markets that appear in the FY2026 to date listings.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are FY2026 obligations by agency?",
        "body": "Lumen Technologies Government Solutions obligations are concentrated among a few agencies. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $75.5M, the Department of Defense obligated $55.2M, the Department of Agriculture obligated $50.7M, and the Department of the Interior obligated $50.2M. The remaining top agencies range from $19.9M down to $2.5M, showing a steep drop after the top four buyers."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does the fiscal-year trend show?",
        "body": "Lumen Technologies Government Solutions obligations rose from $102M in FY21 to $423M in FY25, then moved to $295M in FY26. Obligations are reported as down 30.3% year over year for the current fiscal-year-to-date period."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
